{"title":"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following is an odd integer, contains the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and lies between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/a/5ca7ee3ad271a2c92ed9665f008c2831f5770407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/5/cd54c455a244ae417c0bc931f46d0a3e30b7e79e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/b/adb2ff5521d67d4e7c02ab751808af3e75367966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 105 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 147 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 156 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 165 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 175$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"423\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/b/2ab2b7beba6404117598876178a3c1f171362886.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$156$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Even\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Even\">even</a>, so it cannot be the answer.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b554c3eb69d2f5e6625bd31774ea2be775dd9ec3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$147$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> does not contain the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so it can be eliminated. This means the answer must be A, D, or E.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/4/47466edb148dcae3a1ab096cdaea4f2aed4589d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12^2 = 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85a185cb459b3d034a7ed4428a530d6294a24590.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13^2 = 169$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" />. The only remaining answer that is between those two numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/a/06a854a63e3199738e4d9fd747f37ab90922c4ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D)} 165}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"70\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1999